cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LightWave2D in your research, please cite this software."
title: "LightWave2D"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Poinsinet de Sivry-Houle"
    given-names: "Martin"
abstract: >
  LightWave2D is an open-source Python package for two-dimensional
  finite-difference time-domain simulations of light propagation, scattering,
  diffraction, and photonic components.
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MartinPdeS/LightWave2D"
keywords:
  - finite-difference time-domain
  - light propagation
  - photonics
  - electromagnetics
  - simulation
